From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:03:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0024-developers-text-sjis-and-size

The developers' scenes' text through the US font sheet (PS2_SJIS_TEXT=<texture base>): the scene select (DEBSEL) prints
Shift-JIS strings byte by byte through an ASCII sheet (grey checker boxes and stray letters); a lead byte's sprite is not
drawn and the trail's is moved to the same character's ASCII cell (full-width letters, digits, space, signs, arrows), packed
along its line; kana and kanji pairs are not drawn. While a developers' scene is on screen (set_debug_text, from the
window's PS2_DEBUG_SCENES), the font's 24-pixel letters stretched to 32 with filtering are drawn at their own size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
---
